l-call page doesn't print the tax provision, so `provision_quote` is null.\n- **Her 7 July 2025 press release:** her own words (\"makes the Trump tax cuts permanent, ends taxes on tips and overtime\"). They show the tax-cutting side, but they never say the cut covers \"the main rates most people pay\". They also don't call for cutting \"as far as possible and shrink what government does\", so they don't separate rung 4 from rungs 3 or 5.\n- **Her 22 May 2025 press release:** \"No tax on tips, no tax on overtime, and tax relief for seniors\" is narrow relief, which fits rung 3. Nothing in it rules out a broader cut, so it shows a side only.\n- **Her campaign issues page:** written in the third person (\"Erin believes…\", \"working to cut taxes\"). That makes it someone else describing her, not her own words, so it can't support a chair.\n\n`needs_source` asks for:\n- her own words on cutting the main income-tax rates, or on cutting as far as possible while shrinking government;\n- a single-subject tax bill she wrote or was lead sponsor on that cuts the main income-tax rate.\n\nI included one quote, the 7 July sentence, coded tier `none` and not quotable because it is `not-forward` (it describes what the bill did, not what she would do).","ttft_ms":11570,"type":"result","duration_ms":32629,"uuid":"2918faef-c845-4859-878c-2b0809e6653a","ttft_stream_ms":1178,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":1179,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
